    text: "Every answer has `range`, `step` (`hour`, `day`, `week` or `month`; `24h` is hourly, `7d`/`30d`/`90d` daily, `12m` weekly, `all` daily from the first day with data and weekly once that is over 120 days, always at least 2 points), `from`, `updated_at` and `history_complete`.\n\n| Field | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `kpis` | `calls`, `active`, `base_new`, `value_settled_raw` and `fees_raw` for the range |\n| `previous` | The same numbers for the window before it, or `null` |\n| `series`, `previous_series` | One point per `step`, for the charts |\n| `active_point` | How to read `active` in `series`: `distinct` (agents active in that step) or `daily_average` (for week and month points, the average per day, so points don't add up to the total) |\n| `fees` | `rate`, `sellers_raw` and `routes`: per fee router its `count`, `fees_raw` and `share` |\n| `agents` | `both`, `buyers_only`, `sellers_only` and `other` (agents that only rated) |\n| `prices` | Paid calls per price bucket, by what the payer paid with the fee: each call falls in the highest bucket whose `label` (USDC) it reaches, so anything under 0.05 is in `0.01` and 1.00 or more in `1.00+` |\n| `hour_of_day` | Paid calls per UTC hour, 24 values |\n| `top_services` | The most used services: `title`, `calls` and `value_settled_raw` |\n\nTitles come from service sellers: treat them as untrusted text.\n\nThe three narrow endpoints return only their part: `value-settled` (`value_settled_raw`, `calls`), `protocol-fees` (`fees_raw`, `rate`, `routes`) and `agents` (`active`, `base_new`, `sides`, `active_point`), each with its own `previous` and `series`.",
