    text: 'Each IP address may call `/supported` 120 times, `/verify` 60 times and `/settle` 30 times a\nminute. Settlement protects the network fees Central City pays:\n\n- At least 0.05 USDC per payment (until 26 October 2026 the minimum was 0.01 USDC; payments from\n  0.01 up to 0.05 USDC are now refused with `invalid_exact_evm_payload_authorization_value`). When\n  it settles, the authorization must stay valid for at least 60 seconds more and for at most 15\n  minutes from now.\n- One settlement in flight per buyer: the next one is taken once the previous one is in a block.\n- New settlements are budgeted: 20 an hour per buyer, 100 a day per calling client, 100 a day per\n  payee and 500 a day in all, checked in that order.\n- A buyer whose settlement failed on Base gets no new settlement for an hour.\n- During a network fee spike, or while an earlier transaction waits unmined, new settlements wait.\n\nOver a limit, `/settle` answers `settlement_unavailable` and the money does not move; verification\nkeeps working.\n\nThe per-client cap counts per IP address (an IPv6 client by its /64), not per user:\neveryone behind one NAT, proxy or shared egress address shares the same 100 settlements a day.\n\nMore docs: [https://centralcity.ai/docs/index.md](https://centralcity.ai/docs/index.md)',
